{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"J3 aac8 -> PLAN REVIEW PASS on pass 4 (blocker trajectory 3 -> 1 -> 3 -> 0). CLAIMED.\nPass-3's three blockers were all ONE root cause: the Scope never named the destination file for the relocated map_fields_to_remote, so an implementer had to invent it and AC5's AST assertion had no reachable target. Fixed by naming adapters/jira_family/outbound_mapper.py explicitly and by spelling out that backend.py:59's _JiraOutbound.map_fields_to_remote reduces to a delegation while the NEUTRAL Protocol declaration at _backend.py:117 stays (it is the port contract, not a duplicate).\n\nJ3 ORACLE AUTHORED AND CONFIRMED RED.\n (HAPPY PATH — the only file the implementer sees) test_rich_text_codec.py, 20 tests: the 4-operation contract parameterized over BOTH codecs (round trip, within-limit unchanged/unmarked, over-limit fitted+marked, fit idempotence, decode(None)=='', non-str passthrough), plus Cloud-specific proof that AdfCodec is a PASS-THROUGH to the pinned adf module rather than a reimplementation, that to_wire yields an ADF doc (v3 rejects a bare string with 400), and that the fit measures the SERIALIZED document not the plain text; plus DC-specific character-cap, identity wire shape, and identity normalization.\n (HELD OUT) test_rich_text_seam_heldout.py, 9 tests: Cloud send-path composition parity over 3 input classes; the TWO-CALLERS invariant (sanitizer applies FIT ONLY, backend applies fit THEN normalize — a codec that collapsed them would silently change one); the single-real-map_fields_to_remote AST test that excludes Protocol stubs; and the ADF allowlist (per-file, with a reason recorded for each legitimate site) plus a zero-references assertion over jira_family/ and jira_datacenter/.\nRED EVIDENCE: happy path ModuleNotFoundError on adapters.jira.rich_text_codec (the deliverable). Held out 5 failed / 4 passed — failures are composition parity (module absent), single-implementation (map_fields_to_remote currently lives in adapters/jira/backend.py, not the shared layer), and the ADF allowlist (backend.py and jira_fields.py currently reach for the encoder directly). The 4 that PASS are behavior-preservation invariants that must stay true across the change (sanitizer does not normalize, backend does normalize, non-str bypasses the codec, shared layer names no ADF entry point) — recorded as such rather than 'fixed'.\nSEQUENCING NOTE: deliberately NOT dispatching J3's implementer yet. J4's full-suite run is still in flight, and letting a subagent mutate source files mid-run would invalidate that result. Waiting for the suite, committing J4, then dispatching J3 on top — which is also the correct stack order."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785349935512168001,"uuid":"8bda0ade-9393-4b02-a744-8a61084a906d"}